chongqi and the legend of the ten rings  is finally in theaters worldwide like  any great marvel movie it works on  multiple levels with that in mind here  are a half dozen spoiler heavy lines in  shanxi that mean far more than you might  realize when you first hear them at one  point john john says i speak abc to  katie which many viewers might take as  just a cute way of saying i speak  english in actuality abc is an  abbreviation for american born chinese  writer director destin daniel [ __ ]  said just before the film's release at a  press event attended by looper our  conversation behind which languages  should be spoken was always rooted in  the logic of the characters that  conversation started in the writers room  and then once our actors came in it was  always a dialogue with them is this  character bilingual trilingual  quadrilingual characters could speak  whatever made sense at the time as for  the abc line simu liu who plays shanxi  said the exchange feels very real  explaining abc of course means  american-born chinese it's the first  time that you've seen in a movie someone  just calling that out but it's a lived  experience  early in the movie at an unguarded  moment when the characters are just  living their everyday lives we hear we  are living in a world where any minute  half the population could disappear this  line not only alludes to the wider mcu  universe with plot lines revolving  around thanos and his infamous snap but  also to the mindset of ordinary humans  still grappling years later with the  ramifications although chang chi and the  legend of the ten rings doesn't add any  new names to known victims of the snap  the event touched everyone and it does  make clear that it's still hanging over  the heads of every person on the planet  the general unease of the populace is  backed up by a support group poster that  can be glimpsed next to the door that  shawn enters when he's visiting katie's  family it reads post blip anxiety you  are not alone  the seemingly straightforward line give  me the pendant and no one gets hurt  represents the final moment of sean's  innocence for more than a decade he has  been working to build himself a new life  in san francisco one far away from his  chinese upbringing but as we're about to  see he hasn't been neglecting his  physical fitness when the robber makes  that statement sean could have just  handed over the jade pendant shrugged  his shoulders and katie would likely  think no less of him but that wouldn't  make much of a movie would it does he  look like he can fight come on bro  in a heartbeat shawn launches from  mild-mannered bus patron to full-on  shangqi pulling out acrobatic  environment embracing ass-kicking moves  that would make jackie chan sit up and  applaud in a matter of moments he  doesn't just shatter half the windows on  the bus but also his remaining anonymity  and any pretense of normalcy with friend  katie who watches the whole thing with  her jaw open before finally regaining  enough sense to hop behind the wheel and  drive the bus by the time the scene is  over everything has changed sean has  revealed himself to katie as chongqi his  old life has dragged him back in and he  must go to china to confront his past  also the city of san francisco has a  really big mess to clean up  movies have employed training sequences  for decades but it's another thing to  show and explain in raw detail how day  after day month after month year after  year you were raised to be a killing  machine at one point xiangchi says from  sun up to sundown i was taught every  possible way to kill a man some movies  have the hero adept in martial arts from  the get-go as if it's just something  they picked up others allude to the  training but don't truly depict the full  dedication it requires but by the time  you're finished hearing the tale of  shanxi's upbringing under the tutelage  of his father and the mysterious death  dealer you fully realize how he was able  to mow down those baddies on the bus  keep in mind for almost the entirety of  shanxi and the legend of the ten rings  chang-chi does not have even one ring in  essence he's an unpowered would-be hero  relying solely on his training to battle  a wide array of threats who have  everything from superpowers to at the  bare minimum a machete hand so yes xiang  chi is a trained killer and simulio is  talented enough to sell you on all those  years of training of course by the end  of the movie shanxi does come into  possession of the ten rings so just  imagine how powerful he'll be the next  time we see him in action  when when woo says america was terrified  of an orange some viewers in the  audience may have no clue what the  wearer of the ten rings is talking about  but here's what he's referring to  audiences buying tickets to iron man 3  in 2013 thought they were going to see  tony stark square off against arguably  his arch enemy in the comics the  mandarin like the orange instead they  got guy pierce's aldrich killian as the  man behind the man and ben kingsley as  trevor slattery a british actor  pretending to be the mandarin at the  time some loved the bait and switch  others were disappointed or even flat  out angry as the years went by a third  narrative became the loudest by teasing  a chinese character and instead giving  audiences a white one marvel seemed to  be perpetuating a shameful hollywood  tradition of co-opting and whitewashing  the asian experience marvel head honcho  kevin feige became determined to not  only address such concerns but take back  the mandarin which is why in 2014 marvel  released a one shot called all hail the  king which depicted a post iron man 3  trevor slattery in prison the short film  features a reporter telling slattery  that his portrayal has angered the ten  rings the terrorist group associated  with the real mandarin at the end of the  film the interviewer reveals his true  identity as an agent of the mandarin and  takes slattery prisoner there's somebody  who wants to meet you  don't know him  no  but you took his name  and now he wants it back  which brings us to chongqi when woo's  recounting of the story and the later  revelation that slattery has been held  prisoner ever since in the real  mandarin's dungeon basement  the advice given to katie when she joins  the battle at tallow if you aim at  nothing you hit nothing is more than  just archer mindset as we see at the  beginning of the film sean and katie  were leading a largely aimless existence  valet parking cars for low wages  spending nights drinking and singing  karaoke as katie's family were all too  eager to point out it felt like a road  map to nowhere but what she didn't  realize is that her drinking buddy did  in fact have a purpose even if he was  actively working to suppress it through  chongqi's embracing of his destiny and  her support as a loyal friend the two  characters ended the film with something  to finally aim for a future as  superheroes possibly as avengers and  perhaps katie continuing to embrace her  skills as an archer and car chase driver  if you hang around until the very end of  the credits you'll hear shaling say  let's get started we have a lot of work  to do indicating the donning of a new  day for the character for years her  father wen wu had forbidden her from  training forcing the young girl to  slightly study the men around her and  resolve to be even more effective in her  movements later in life she'd become  disappointed by another man when brother  xiang chi left her behind in china now  after the heroes won the day at talo and  her father is no longer a threat to  contend with chiang chi has taken the 10  rings and once again left this time for  a new life of adventure in san francisco  and the sanctum sanctorum this leaves  xia ling alone to rebuild and rule over  a new kingdom which is where we find her  in this end credit scene surrounded by  people training for battle where will  this new chapter take her it's hard to  tell because in the comics there is no  shaolin but shaolin could be based on  the cursed lotus a super villain who's  the older half-sister of chongqi in the  comics the cursed lotus was a gifted  hand-to-hand combatant and seductress  who longed to follow in her father's  footsteps and led her own criminal  organization called the oriental  expediters although there's an extremely  good chance that name will not be  appearing in the mcu it's possible that  the people we see training under her  tutelage are early expediters and as  we've already seen from shaolin's  prominence in the underground fighting  community she knows plenty of tough  folks who would likely be for hire we  almost certainly haven't seen the last  of shaolin and chongqi better be  prepared for another smackdown with sis  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite mcu movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

